 "summary": "annotateEffectiveApiOperations (packages/core/src/security/effective-object-permissions.ts) now asks the REST door's own two questions per entry. Object half: canServeApiOperation, the boolean face of the spec's apiExposureDenialReason, which enforceApiAccess turns into 404/405, so an enable.apiEnabled:false object is annotated [] instead of its whole closure or no annotation. Export half: objectPermissionGrants(entry, 'allowExport'), which is read AND grant on the entry itself (per set and posture since #20083/#20134), in place of the merged '*' export bit; this closes pointer 5831905897. Unchanged: the REST door, packages/spec, checkObjectPermission, the seed, the folds, and every exported name and type. Card assignee os-sales was set at dispatch and mirrored onto the PR. Claim verified: the newest Claim (5833697522) names this branch.",
 "tests": "All at head f2904cd05b, core dist rebuilt from source, each under os-verify-lock with VERDICT command-exit 0. (1) pnpm --filter @objectstack/core test: 53 files / 1353 passed, typecheck exit 0. (2) pnpm --filter @objectstack/plugin-hono-server test: 27 files / 323 passed, typecheck exit 0. (3) pnpm --filter @objectstack/plugin-security test: 135 files / 2718 passed, typecheck exit 0. (4) Dogfood, 18 access-security files, against the turbo-built dogfood^... closure (64 tasks): first run 126 passed, 1 skipped (organization-update-door, me-apps-and-everyone-baseline, showcase-permission-projection, showcase-permission-seeding, showcase-permission-zoo, two-doors-permission, comments-permission-matrix, attachments-permission-matrix, authz-conformance); second run 135 passed (showcase-private-owd, owner-anchor-and-bulk-writes, showcase-crud-persona-matrix, showcase-client-liaison-fixtures, showcase-fls-read-mask-strip, showcase-scope-depth, showcase-scope-depth-write, showcase-scope-depth-fallback, showcase-anonymous-deny-surfaces). ABLATION through scripts/ablation-replace.mjs: one block restoring the base reading (the merged '*' export bit, no door filter) plus a string marker. Anchor 1 → 0, blob da81b319 → 33501e91, core dist rebuilt, ablation-dist-preflight found the marker in 2 built files. Direction: RED. core 5 failed / 22 passed (the 2 right-direction controls stayed green). hono 6 failed / 27 passed. plugin-security 16 failed / 36 passed (15 subject rows of the apiOperations column plus the reported-cases case; every can() row green). Restore: blob == HEAD and git diff HEAD empty (tool verdict); core rebuilt; ablation-dist-preflight --absent reports the marker absent from all 14 built files and a clean tree; suites green again 27/33/52. A second ablation leg dumped both legs' maps and restored the same way. Throwaway stack probe (bootStack, real /auth/me/permissions route and real REST routes) was run at base 16c5a33fdd, on the ablated build (its door