 "mcp_calls": "0: no MCP GitHub tool was called. Reads went through REST GET with the session token: issue 20135, its comments, issues 18931/18990/20136, PRs 20132/20145, and PR 20151 read-back.",
 "api_writes": "3, each one fleet-write relay dispatch (POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/dispatches) executed as objectstack-fleet[bot]: (1) pr_create, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/pulls (draft #20151, relay run 36152948654); (2) label-write --assign os-sales, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/20151/assignees (relay run 36153046523, read back as matching); (3) this os-dev-report comment, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/20135/comments. There were 4 git pushes to the branch; those are not REST writes.",
 "open_questions": [
  {
   "question": "Three pending changesets in this release describe an unrestricted, export-allowed object as carrying no apiOperations: 18931 ('an object that is unrestricted and keeps export gets none'), 18990 ('an unrestricted object whose export stays allowed still gets no apiOperations') and 20134 ('That entry carries no apiOperations'). At this head an API-disabled one carries []. Those files are outside the claimed surface, so they were not edited. Correct them?",
   "options": [
    "A: leave them. This PR's changeset states the exception explicitly in the same release, and the release notes are compiled together.",
    "B: DELIBERATE CORRECTION of one clause in each, in this PR. This needs a claim amendment for the three files, and check-empty-changeset goes red on the foreign-changeset rule by design, as in the #20132/#20145 precedent."
   ],
   "recommendation": "A. Read with 'keeps export' meaning 'the door serves export', each sentence stays true, and the one exception is named in this release's own note. B costs a red gate and a prose review for no reader-visible gain. If the seat reads the sentences literally, B is a three-line change."
  },
  {
   "question": "annotateEffectiveApiOperations is an exported helper. Called standalone on a map that never went through buildEffectiveObjectPermissions, it no longer inherits the map's '*' export bit. Does Clause-2 stay 'no' / core patch?",
   "options": [
    "A: keep 'no' and patch as the claim declares. There are 0 non-test callers in the repo, the helper is a pass of the one composition, and the changeset names the behaviour change.",
    "B: grade it as a narrowing of a published helper: 'no (narrowing)', BREAKING."
   ],
   "recommendation": "A. The served response only narrows toward what the door already refuses (0 operations added, measured). No request changes its answer, and the helper's documented role is the composition's last pass. check-changeset-no-major and check-adr-0087-registration both exit 0."
  }
 ],
 "out_of_scope_findings": [
  "carrier: #20136's taker, or the domain:engine seat, for the entry-presence question. Noted, not filed. On the stack, subjects with no entry for an object leave the client on default-allow for operations the door refuses: member_default 134 cells, the member-with-read rows 101, the plain-wildcard member 15. The counts are identical at base and head. Every such object is one the subject cannot read at all (can() reads 'no grant'), so no affordance is reachable. That makes it an observation, not class a.",
  "carrier: none. Noted, not filed. The spec describe string on EffectiveObjectPermissionSchema.apiOperations ('Present only when the object tightens exposure via apiMethods') has been inexact since the export axis (#3544) and now also for apiEnabled:false. packages/spec was out of scope. This is documentation drift, in Acceptance notes.",
  "carrier: none. Noted, not filed. For an unrestricted object the spec's apiExposureDenialReason admits history/restore/purge/search, while resolveEffectiveApiMethods withholds the flag-gated ones. No REST route gates those by name, so nothing is reachable. It is outside the parity column by construction, in Acceptance notes."
 ],
 "gates": "Derived at head f2904cd05b by node scripts/pm/dispatch-gates.mjs --commands --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack (no paths): 64 commands from 6 paths vs merge base 16c5a33fd. 64/64 exit 0. pnpm check:dual-build-cjs-loads first returned exit 3 PREREQUISITE NOT MET (8 packages had no dist); after turbo build of those 8 (all cache hits) it passed: 105 entries across 67 packages load, 660 CJS files parse. dispatch-gates --ran: 64 derived, 64 run, 0 NOT-MEASURED, 0 UNRUN. node scripts/check-issue-citations.mjs --base 16c5a33fdd: exit 0, 3 citations resolve. check-changeset-no-major --base origin/main: exit 0 ('no major bump'). check-adr-0087-registration --base origin/main: exit 0 ('1 non-breaking changeset(s) seen'). Control-byte self-scan over the 6 files: 0 hits. Lint, as a proven narrowing: eslint --no-inline-config --format json over the 5 changed TS files gives 5 files, 0 errors, 0 warnings. --print-config resolves each of them, and eslint ignores the changeset. eslint.config.mjs enables no type-aware linting (no parserOptions.project, as its own comment at L327-328 states), so no untouched file's verdict can move. NOT MEASURED, CI-owned: Test Core, Dogfood Regression Gate, Build Core, Temporal Conformance, the type-check lanes, the repo-wide pnpm lint, and the families dispatch-gates lists outside its 64.",
 "line_budget": "n/a: no skills/** in the diff",
 "deviations": [
  "plugin-hono-server effective-api-operations.test.ts: 4 existing cases rewritten. One is INVERTED on purpose (it pinned the merged-'*' export fallback itself). Three called annotate on maps that never went through the per-set passes, so they now go through buildEffectiveObjectPermissions with the same assertions. All inside the claimed hono test side.",
  "The committed parity column's object-door oracle is canServeApiOperation (@objectstack/spec/data), the function the REST door's apiAccessDenialFromEnable wraps. plugin-security has no @objectstack/rest dependency, and adding one is outside the claimed surface. The export half uses the real registered svc.canExport. The real REST door was measured by the throwaway stack probe.",
