 },
 "disabled_shape": "apiOperations: [] and the entry stays. Reading: nothing in this repo's SDK reads apiOperations (git grep over packages/client and packages/client-react gives 0; @objectstack/client only re-exports the GetEffectivePermissionsResponse type). The reader is objectui, UNMEASURED here (not in the container). Per the spec contract ('absent = default-allow') and the objectui gate quoted on #18931 (effectiveApiOps ? effectiveApiOps.includes('export') : true), an array hides whatever it omits and absence hides nothing. [] is already the deny-all (apiMethods: []) shape. Dropping the entry would flip server-side current_user.can() to 'no grant' for data the subject may still write through internal paths (apiEnabled closes the API, not data access). That is a server-decision change H5 forbids, and it contradicts the #18990 ruling that every reachable object gets an entry.",
 "reach": "H1 CONFIRMED on the real public door. bootStack with the real SecurityPlugin and an authored app (0 apiEnabled:false objects exist in examples/). At base 16c5a33fdd the seeded platform admin's GET /auth/me/permissions annotated pq_hidden (enable.apiEnabled:false, no apiMethods) with [get, list, create, update, delete, upsert, bulk, aggregate, search, import], while every REST verb on it answered 404 OBJECT_API_DISABLED. For export-allowed subjects the entry had no annotation at all (default-allow). ISecurityService.getEffectiveObjectPermissions was byte-equal to the route in all 8 subjects. Controls: pq_open and pq_exposed (apiEnabled absent or true) matched the door; pq_subset (apiMethods get/list) matched at base and head. At head every API-disabled entry reads [] and all 8 subjects show 0 present-entry mismatches in both directions. H2 CONFIRMED: admin_full_access beside a plain '*' allowExport had sys_secret annotated export while the export route answered 403 EXPORT_NOT_PERMITTED; the authored private pq_private had the same over-offer through default-allow, and so did the member-with-read beside the plain export wildcard. H5: no server decision and no exported type changed, Clause-2 no, core patch; both gates exit 0."
